# T041 Reviewed Diff Manifest

T041 reviews the complete feature 009 implementation recorded by T038 through
T040 together with copied-out generation, canonical React assets, CI and release
automation, current documentation, delivery governance, and corrective acceptance
work. Published Alpha 3 tags and downstream Rulary source are outside the diff.

The reviewed implementation contains:

- separate root, ordinary PostgreSQL, governed PostgreSQL/River, and integration
  modules with selection-sensitive generated dependency graphs;
- immutable pre-start HTTP/Admin contribution contracts with bounded capability,
  route, descriptor, and permission metadata;
- provider-neutral task/audit readers, schema-role coordination, indexed cursor
  queries, and precision-safe wire IDs;
- generated Chinese React Admin records, optional task/audit surfaces, shared
  work primitives, permission-aware module resolution, deterministic selected
  assets, and desktop/mobile accessibility behavior;
- copied-out default and operations Admin CI with real PostgreSQL and frozen
  frontend pipelines, plus required copied-out Governed PostgreSQL/River tests;
- full-field backend descriptor assertions and direct records list/create/update/
  delete denial tests;
- deterministic role-prefixed Starter schema derivation with separate 63-byte
  PostgreSQL and 46-byte River limits, reserved-schema avoidance, independently
  bounded test schemas, stable hash suffixes, and maximum/reserved-sensitive
  copied-out PostgreSQL/River runtime acceptance;
- pre-write rejection of Go Module Paths containing a `vendor` segment;
- early River queue-schema boundary validation; and
- a canonical-root candidate-source digest that makes stale T041 evidence fail
  documentation and release gates without caller-root, relative-path, or symlink
  bypasses.

The repeat plan uses an 8-minute package timeout with explicitly curated Core,
Starter, component, integration, and copied-out consumer contracts. It does not
claim blanket repetition of static packages.
